body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-11 11:01 PST (session 3d705fec): still open, unclaimed; REB still has 0 versions (read-only check 11:01 PST). Attempted to create version `rebar-fixver-probe` in REB under the operator's recorded pre-authorization (memory production-writes-preauthorized; settings.local.json autoMode.allow). The official acli has no version-create command, so the route is Jira REST `POST /rest/api/3/version` with the configured identity (holds ADMINISTER_PROJECTS on REB). Claude Code's auto-mode permission check blocked that call as an external-system write before it ran, so nothing was written. Next: once the operator allows that REST call (or creates the version), create it, record who/when/how here, check the plan-review cert, claim, and run the round trip.","timestamp":1794423738741250869},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Live evidence 2026-11-11 PST (session 3d705fec). Production bridge = .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml on main; every run below has a head SHA descending from b878c4be768 (checked with git merge-base --is-ancestor). Each run was dispatched (gh workflow run) after the triggering write reached origin/tickets. REB versions re-checked at 16:16 PST: [] (read-only GET /rest/api/3/project/REB/versions).\n\nProbe: centauric-bony-impala (cf6d-5d0a-dfb4-4b8b), created via MCP create_ticket with bridge_project=REB, tagged probe, parent this ticket. Pushed to tickets 16:17:27 PST.\n\n1. Binding — run 43126417285 (head c80576dfdb3, 16:19:16-16:26:26 PST, success). .bridge_state/bindings.json on origin/tickets: bindings[cf6d-5d0a-dfb4-4b8b].jira_key = REB-7117. GET /rest/api/3/issue/REB-7117: summary \"[probe] fix-version sync check (plucky-jetblack-parrot) - safe to close\", fixVersions [], status To Do. Log: \"RECON: outbound_differ total=18 create=1\".\n2. Withhold — `rebar edit centauric-bony-impala --add-release rebar-fixver-probe` (worktree CLI; the production MCP edit_ticket does not yet expose add_releases, see reddish-drinkable-canvasback), pushed 16:28:07 PST. Run 43127503834 (head c80576dfdb3, 16:28:14-16:36:41 PST, success). rebar show: releases ['rebar-fixver-probe']; bridge_alerts [release-version-missing:rebar-fixver-probe, resolved False, uuid c00be723-e97c-4670-846e-d3e6606bf3a1]. GET REB-7117 fixVersions: []. Log: \"RECON: outbound_update key=REB-7117 changed=[] comments=1 labels=0 links=0 releases=0\" (no fixVersions write; no \"fix version add failed\" line; no release_alerts version-read warning).\n3. Steady state / retry — run 43128646371 (head c80576dfdb3, 16:37:34-16:45:10 PST, success). Probe events on origin/tickets before 3, after 3 (CREATE, RELEASE_DELTA, BRIDGE_ALERT). Alert still unresolved; GET fixVersions []. Log: \"outbound_update key=REB-7117 ... releases=0\"; no version-read warning, so availability was known and the withholding re-ran.\n4. Resolution — `rebar edit centauric-bony-impala --remove-release rebar-fixver-probe`, pushed 16:46:09 PST. Run 43129719419 (head fdf0a94aba8, 16:46:16-17:03:35 PST, success). rebar show: releases []; alert release-version-missing:rebar-fixver-probe resolved True (new BRIDGE_ALERT event 767a643e). GET REB-7117 fixVersions [].\n5. Follow-up for the version-dependent checks (Jira->rebar, a release written to Jira, ADR 0124 screen question): cognitive-sooty-angelfish, parent the epic, linked discovered_from this ticket.\nNote: the production MCP server's edit_ticket lacks add_releases/remove_releases because its code workspace lags main (reddish-drinkable-canvasback).","timestamp":1794445556838021118},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-11 17:27 PST (session 3d705fec): CLOSED (completion gate passed after a re-review, needed because the probe child changed the plan material). Evidence is in the comment above (runs 43126417285, 43127503834, 43128646371, 43129719419; REB-7117). Probe centauric-bony-impala closed as obsolete (\"probe complete\"). Version-dependent checks continue in cognitive-sooty-angelfish.","timestamp":1794446870218869496}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794256491357459001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7c5f8665-69d3-4b92-a0e3-c9863244a21a","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"ed07-b103-3e7b-4c50"},{"link_uuid":"e1507571-64e8-4915-824c-b67e24ef5c04","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"ed07-b103-3e7b-4c50"},{"link_uuid":"27cf7d62-93f2-4566-bf74-46ed98772a1a","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"15e2-68c2-fab2-4cbd"},{"link_uuid":"5ee31d1a-28dc-4f87-bbc7-00c3a4655f3b","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"15e2-68c2-fab2-4cbd"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe epic's last criterion is a live check of the fix-version sync on the production bridge. Every earlier child is pinned by tests over recorded or documented payloads only. Project REB has no Jira versions (read-only checks 2026-11-10 and 2026-11-11 PST), and the bridge never creates one (ADR 0124 decision 8). The operator ruled (2026-11-11) that this check runs through rebar itself: a probe ticket created in rebar syncs to REB, and its `releases` are set and changed through rebar. With REB holding no versions, the live path that rebar provides is the missing-version path (child gymnasial-snappy-lorikeet): a rebar release is withheld from Jira, kept on the ticket, alerted, retried each pass, and the alert resolves when the release no longer needs writing. Writing a version into Jira, and the Jira→rebar direction, need a version that exists in REB; those stay pinned by the recorded-payload tests of the inbound and outbound children, and their live check is split into a follow-up task that starts once REB has a people-created version.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **Deploy.** The production bridge is `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml` (hourly at :23 on `main`, `pip install .` from the checkout, plus manual dispatch). Record the first run whose head SHA contains b878c4be768 (all code children).\n2. **Probe ticket.** Create a task through the rebar MCP `create_ticket` (or the worktree CLI) with `bridge_project=\"REB\"`, title `[probe] fix-version sync check (plucky-jetblack-parrot) - safe to close`, and a description saying it is a test artifact. After the next completed run it is bound to a new REB issue: read the key from `bindings[<probe id>].jira_key` in `.bridge_state/bindings.json` on the `tickets` branch (`git show origin/tickets:.bridge_state/bindings.json`), confirm it with the run log's outbound create line, and record it with the run id; `rebar show` confirms `bridge_project: REB`.\n3. **rebar→Jira, missing version.** `edit_ticket(probe, add_releases=[\"rebar-fixver-probe\"])` through MCP. After the next completed run: `rebar show` lists `releases: [\"rebar-fixver-probe\"]` and one unresolved `BRIDGE_ALERT` with reason `release-version-missing:rebar-fixver-probe`; a read-only `GET /rest/api/3/issue/<KEY>?fields=fixVersions` returns `[]`; the run log has no `fix version add failed` line for the key.\n4. **Steady state and retry.** The following completed run writes no new event on the probe (event count from the tracker before and after) and no `fixVersions` write for the key, and the alert stays unresolved.\n5. **Resolution.** `edit_ticket(probe, remove_releases=[\"rebar-fixver-probe\"])`. After the next completed run the alert is resolved and the Jira issue's `fixVersions` is still `[]`.\n6. **Follow-up.** Create a task, linked `discovered_from` this ticket, for the live checks that need an existing REB version (Jira→rebar sync, a rebar release written to Jira), to run once a person creates one.\n7. **Record and close.** One comment with run ids, PST times and outputs; close the probe ticket as obsolete with reason \"probe complete\" so its REB issue follows.\n\n## Scope\n\nNo repository files change: this is a live production check. Evidence lives in comments on this ticket and the epic.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] [non-codebase] The probe ticket created in rebar is bound to a REB issue after a completed bridge run on a `main` commit containing b878c4be768.\n  provenance: environment=production reconcile-bridge.yml on main; principal=bridge Jira account; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — run id, head SHA and the REB key from `.bridge_state/bindings.json` on the tickets branch\n- [x] [non-codebase] A rebar release naming a version REB lacks is withheld: after the next run the ticket keeps it, carries one unresolved `release-version-missing:<name>` alert, and the Jira issue's `fixVersions` is `[]`.\n  provenance: environment=production bridge and Jira Cloud REB; principal=bridge account (writes), configured Jira identity (read-only GET); privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — run id, `rebar show` and REST excerpts\n- [x] [non-codebase] The following run writes no event on the probe and no `fixVersions` change, and the alert stays unresolved.\n  provenance: environment=production bridge; principal=bridge account; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — run id, tracker event counts, run log\n- [x] [non-codebase] Removing the release in rebar resolves the alert after the next run.\n  provenance: environment=production bridge; principal=bridge account; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — run id and `rebar show` excerpt\n- [x] A follow-up task for the version-dependent live checks exists, linked `discovered_from` this ticket.\n","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["depends_on","15e2-68c2-fab2-4cbd"],["depends_on","ed07-b103-3e7b-4c50"],["parent","21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"Why no repository files change: this is a live production check of the reconcile bridge against Jira. Where output or evidence lives: run ids, PST times and command output recorded in comments on this ticket and the epic.","parent_id":"21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775","parent_status_uuid":"4f48ba65-5ef2-405e-ba1c-8490b92794fd","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"80c7-7d3a-158e-4845","ticket_type":"task","title":"Verify release sync both ways on the production bridge","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a4d67424-8e92-4ebc-9101-b022ad6b06a1","017a2b49-7852-40c7-9ad5-e9137bc5953c","d45687d5-dda9-49bb-9c21-035e7a3cca68","4e582ada-33ce-4782-a9f0-ddf3005f821d","6414af41-fffa-423b-aac9-b845128d8095","a55a7c24-b198-4ab5-91b1-291eab9d0bb0","0403f2f8-1fbd-48c7-8702-20b9c59661c8","9ece13fb-d71a-48d3-ace1-33a38e08469c","b3aecf15-ca38-4661-9832-7e26dd13e24d","32ae1600-eae2-4a94-a8bd-08eae4d81c2b","4f48ba65-5ef2-405e-ba1c-8490b92794fd","0e2cf18e-9b72-4622-8af0-bc8670d694d0","c2cc8f89-b6eb-4929-b7d2-8051e739478a"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794446870218869497,"uuid":"6726a954-9448-4431-88be-314d52633d4c"}